  "tutorial": {
    "steps": {
      "intro": "Defeat the opposing mage to win. The Beastmaster builds mana, prepares spells, summons creatures, then uses position and attacks to pressure the enemy.",
      "selfHud": "The Beastmaster has 24 life, 10 channeling, and a mana pool. Mana pays for summons and incantations; damage up to your life total means defeat.",
      "stage": "The phase track shows where the round is. Preparation phases advance after both players confirm; action phases resolve in player order.",
      "advanceChannel": "Click “End Turn” to finish reset. Once both players confirm, channeling gives the Beastmaster this round's mana income.",
      "channelResult": "Channeling adds 10 mana. This round you can summon Jungle Wolf and still keep an incantation ready so it can act at once.",
      "advanceUpkeep": "Upkeep resolves ongoing effects and status. There is no upkeep cost in this position, so click “End Turn” to continue into planning.",
      "advancePlanning": "During planning, secretly prepare up to two spellbook cards. Click “End Turn” to open this round's spell choice.",
      "planWolf": "Choose the Creature category, go to the next page, and select “Jungle Wolf”; then switch to Incantation, go to the next page, select “Rouse the Beast”, and click “Prepare 2”. This pair turns a summon into immediate pressure.",
      "preparedAndHidden": "Your two prepared spells are below; the opponent also has hidden prepared spells. A spell moves to discard after it is cast and revealed.",
      "deployWolf": "Choose “Jungle Wolf” in your prepared spells, then click the Beastmaster's zone to summon it. A newly summoned creature enters play with its action marker spent.",
      "rouseWolf": "Choose “Rouse the Beast” in your prepared spells, then click Jungle Wolf in the arena. The incantation readies a living creature summoned this round.",
      "passYourDeployment": "Jungle Wolf is ready to act. After your deployment ends, the opponent will reveal prepared spells of their own.",
      "opponentDeploy": "The opponent summons Asyran Cleric. Revealed enemy creatures stay in the arena, where you can read life, armor, and damage.",
      "opponentAttackSpell": "The opponent casts Pillar of Light at the cleric. Spell attacks show dice, damage, and any status that appears.",
      "discardReading": "The discard pile records spells that were revealed and resolved. Seeing Pillar of Light there tells you one attack spell is gone.",
      "skipToCreatureAction": "After both quickcast windows are passed, the round enters creature actions. The roused Jungle Wolf can still move.",
      "moveWolf": "Click Jungle Wolf, then click an adjacent zone to move it. After moving, the wolf is closer to the center line and threatens more targets.",
      "finish": "You have completed a basic round: channel mana, prepare spells, summon, rouse, read public information, and move a creature into a stronger position."
    }
